# platform.linux.storage.absent

An explicit unavailable SD socket for Linux SDL boards. Applications can
select their SD volume and receive Unsupported without requiring storage
emulation or a physical card provider. The same module supplies an unavailable
FAT and LittleFS providers so applications can link without those storage
backends on this board.
